selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#think-python-cymraeg\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Think Python \u2192 Cymraeg<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#think-python-cymraeg\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h1><p>Welsh translation of <em>Think Python</em>, 3rd edition (Allen B. Downey, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0),\nfor free distribution to UK higher-education students \u2014 target audience is year 2 CS\nundergrads who\u2019ve completed C and Java modules. Hosted on GitHub Pages from this repo\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">waubrey/think-python-cy</span></code>).</p>", "a[href=\"#build\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Build<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#build\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Always check the build output for warnings \u2014 <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">WARNING:</span> <span class=\"pre\">term</span> <span class=\"pre\">not</span> <span class=\"pre\">in</span> <span class=\"pre\">glossary:</span> <span class=\"pre\">'X'</span></code>\nmeans a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">{term}</span></code>\u2026`` role was added in a chapter but the matching entry was never\nadded to <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">glossary.md</span></code>, and a cross-reference warning means a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(label)=</span></code> anchor is\nmissing or misplaced. Grep output with:</p>", "a[href=\"#translation-conventions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Translation conventions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#translation-conventions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><h3>Gotcha: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">{term}</span></code> roles must match the glossary headword exactly<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#gotcha-term-roles-must-match-the-glossary-headword-exactly\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Sphinx-tippy links a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">{term}</span></code>word<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"> <span class=\"pre\">role</span> <span class=\"pre\">to</span> <span class=\"pre\">its</span> <span class=\"pre\">glossary</span> <span class=\"pre\">entry</span> <span class=\"pre\">by</span> <span class=\"pre\">exact</span> <span class=\"pre\">text</span> <span class=\"pre\">match.</span> <span class=\"pre\">A</span> <span class=\"pre\">mutated</span> <span class=\"pre\">Welsh</span> <span class=\"pre\">form</span> <span class=\"pre\">(treiglad)</span> <span class=\"pre\">\u2014</span> <span class=\"pre\">e.g.</span> <span class=\"pre\">`{term}`ddosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code> when the glossary\nheadword is <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code> \u2014 breaks the link and produces a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">WARNING:</span> <span class=\"pre\">term</span> <span class=\"pre\">not</span> <span class=\"pre\">in</span> <span class=\"pre\">glossary</span></code> build warning even though the entry exists. Fix by\nrewording the sentence to avoid triggering the mutation inside the role (e.g. swap\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">yn</span> <span class=\"pre\">ddosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code> for <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fel</span> <span class=\"pre\">dosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code>), not by adding a duplicate glossary\nentry for the mutated form.</p>", "a[href=\"#where-things-live\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Where things live<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#where-things-live\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#gotcha-term-roles-must-match-the-glossary-headword-exactly\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Gotcha: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">{term}</span></code> roles must match the glossary headword exactly<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#gotcha-term-roles-must-match-the-glossary-headword-exactly\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>Sphinx-tippy links a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">{term}</span></code>word<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"> <span class=\"pre\">role</span> <span class=\"pre\">to</span> <span class=\"pre\">its</span> <span class=\"pre\">glossary</span> <span class=\"pre\">entry</span> <span class=\"pre\">by</span> <span class=\"pre\">exact</span> <span class=\"pre\">text</span> <span class=\"pre\">match.</span> <span class=\"pre\">A</span> <span class=\"pre\">mutated</span> <span class=\"pre\">Welsh</span> <span class=\"pre\">form</span> <span class=\"pre\">(treiglad)</span> <span class=\"pre\">\u2014</span> <span class=\"pre\">e.g.</span> <span class=\"pre\">`{term}`ddosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code> when the glossary\nheadword is <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code> \u2014 breaks the link and produces a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">WARNING:</span> <span class=\"pre\">term</span> <span class=\"pre\">not</span> <span class=\"pre\">in</span> <span class=\"pre\">glossary</span></code> build warning even though the entry exists. Fix by\nrewording the sentence to avoid triggering the mutation inside the role (e.g. swap\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">yn</span> <span class=\"pre\">ddosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code> for <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fel</span> <span class=\"pre\">dosbarth</span> <span class=\"pre\">rhiant</span></code>), not by adding a duplicate glossary\nentry for the mutated form.</p>", "a[href=\"#status\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Status<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#status\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>All 19 chapters are translated, built, and pushed. The book builds with zero warnings.\nOutstanding: the \ud83d\udfe1 \u201creasoned\u201d glossary terms (see below) haven\u2019t been checked by a\nWelsh-medium CS teacher or CBAC yet \u2014 that\u2019s the one piece of this project that needs\na human, not Claude.</p>", "a[href=\"#next-step\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Next step<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#next-step\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Get the \ud83d\udfe1 terms in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">TERMINOLOGY.md</span></code> checked by a Welsh-medium CS teacher or CBAC\u2019s\nsubject officer (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">cyfrifiadureg@cbac.co.uk</span></code>). Highest priority: <em>priodoledd</em>\n(attribute), <em>Adeiladydd</em> (constructor), and <em>enghraifft</em> (instance) \u2014 these recur in\nnearly every chapter from 14 onward, so confirming just these three de-risks most of\nthe book.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 500, interactive: false,

            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
